[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813710807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114941#issuecomment-3813710807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114941","id":3813710807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jUJvX","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T20:16:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T20:19:33Z","body":"If I'm not mistaken with some tests I did, currently (Godot 4.5.1) java lists and arrays are accessible as `JavaObject`, not godot `Array`. Which btw is particularly complicated in the case of arrays, as you can't call indexer like `array[i]` from GDScript. List is a little less of an issue since you can do `list.call(&'get', i)` I believe.\r\n\r\nWill this PR change behavior so all java maps are accessible in GDScript as a Godot `Dictionary` instead of a `JavaObject`? Because if so, it would be inconsistent with `Array` if the same is not done to convert java arrays and/or collections into godot arrays.\r\n\r\nI think either everything should be converted, or better yet only java arrays into godot `Array[JavaObject]` and lists/collections and maps remain as `JavaObject` as you can do everything via methods and field access.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813710807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814015622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114941#issuecomment-3814015622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114941","id":3814015622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jVUKG","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T21:25:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T21:25:55Z","body":"> If I'm not mistaken with some tests I did, currently (Godot 4.5.1) java lists and arrays are accessible as `JavaObject`, not godot `Array`. Which btw is particularly complicated in the case of arrays, as you can't call indexer like `array[i]` from GDScript. List is a little less of an issue since you can do `list.call(&'get', i)` I believe.\r\n> \r\n> Will this PR change behavior so all java maps are accessible in GDScript as a Godot `Dictionary` instead of a `JavaObject`? Because if so, it would be inconsistent with `Array` if the same is not done to convert java arrays and/or collections into godot arrays.\r\n> \r\n> I think either everything should be converted, or better yet only java arrays into godot `Array[JavaObject]` and lists/collections and maps remain as `JavaObject` as you can do everything via methods and field access.\r\n\r\n@geekley Let's continue this conversation in the linked issue to keep the PR focused on the Map / HashMap implementation. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814015622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814302008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114941#issuecomment-3814302008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114941","id":3814302008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jWaE4","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https